  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires rapid reporting and customer notification, with no delay for verification. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% limit but allows continued sale under a time-limited regulator-approved mitigation plan with no fixed duration or interim cap; per-model results go to customers and regulators but not the public. S3 mandates remote shut-off for new units in 24 months and retrofit in 72 months with a feasibility escape requiring alternative mitigation. S4 requires built-in or validated equivalent suppression at 36 months. S5 sets a mandatory 8/100k recall trigger with immediate notices, no serious-injury clause, and no transition."
